{% comment %}
  TRMNL private plugin markup — voice chess board.
  Modeled on the Lichess Daily Puzzle layout: the board is a single remote
  image, so no CSS board and no dithering problems.

  merge_variables pushed by chess_mcp_server.py:
    image_url, status, last_move, move_number, turn, player_color, history,
    engine, level, white_captured, black_captured, white_edge, black_edge

  The board image is oriented to player_color (the user's own pieces at the
  bottom), so it's worth always showing player_color on-screen too -- without
  it, a flipped board with no label is confusing rather than clarifying.

  white_captured/black_captured are Unicode chess glyphs for the pieces
  that side has captured (confirmed live: the glyphs render correctly on
  real TRMNL hardware). white_edge/black_edge are the material lead ("+3")
  shown only next to whichever side is ahead.

  LAYOUT NOTE: this is the original single layout--col structure, kept
  exactly as it was when it worked cleanly. Two multi-column rewrites (a
  hand-rolled layout--row, then TRMNL's own .columns/.column) both pushed
  total content height past the fixed 800x480 canvas and clipped the
  header and/or dropped the history line entirely -- confirmed via
  screenshots on real hardware both times. The captured-pieces line below
  is added as one more row in the SAME proven vertical stack, not a new
  side-by-side structure, specifically to avoid that failure mode again.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="layout layout--col gap--small lg:gap">

  <div class="flex flex--row flex--between flex--center-y">
    <span class="label label--base lg:label--large">
      Move {{ move_number }} — {{ turn }} to play
    </span>
    <span class="label label--outline label--base lg:label--large">
      {{ engine }} · {{ level }}
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex--center-x flex--center-y stretch-y" style="overflow:hidden;">
    <img style="max-width:100%; max-height:90cqh; object-fit:contain;"
         src="{{ image_url }}" alt="Chess board">
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex--row flex--between flex--center-y">
    <span class="label label--small">
      White {{ white_captured }}{% if white_edge != "" %} {{ white_edge }}{% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="label label--small">
      Black {{ black_captured }}{% if black_edge != "" %} {{ black_edge }}{% endif %}
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex--center-x">
    <span class="label label--base lg:label--base">
      {% for move in history %}{{ move }}{% unless forloop.last %} · {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
    </span>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="title">Voice Chess — playing {{ player_color }}</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ last_move }} · {{ status }} · {{ engine }} {{ level }}</span>
</div>
